# Cloudflare Pages cache rules.
#
# The HTML is the index of which asset versions to load, so it must never be
# staler than the assets it points at. It was max-age=600 while the JS was
# max-age=14400 — a browser could hold a four-hour-old mutra-page.js against a
# ten-minute-old HTML, which is exactly how someone ends up running a player
# that predates a fix and hearing a watermark that was removed hours ago.
#
# So: HTML always revalidates, and the versioned assets it names can then be
# cached hard, because a change to any of them changes the ?v= in the HTML.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
